Subject: Cantor Recursive Machine Schema Constraint Ledger

@ [ledger_uuid] 158651e8-d1de-4816-9986-e8bd7e173b6e

& [Must] is fail closed
  + emit ProcedureType and ProcedureValue exactly once in shared definitions
  + use only fragment-local references beginning with #/
  + reject any scheme, authority, absolute path, relative file, or network reference
  + canonicalize and digest the finite document without dereferencing cycles
  + traverse definitions with visited and active sets and finite global counters
  + retain serde decode and Cantor maximum_call_depth as separate residual enforcement
  + test direct self cycles, unexpected mutual cycles, unresolved local targets, forbidden external references, and boundary-depth instances

& [MustNot] preserves compatibility
  - never: unroll recursion to a fixed schema depth
  - never: introduce a replacement ProcedureValue wire form
  - never: disable serde_json recursion limits
  - never: claim JSON Schema enforces semantic maximum_call_depth
  - never: fetch or resolve a reference outside the in-memory canonical bundle
  - never: let cycle traversal evade definition, reference, property, byte, or work counters

& [StopConditions] are exact
  + stop I02 if schemars output cannot preserve stable local type names
  + stop I02 if generated recursion disagrees with actual serde tags or closed-object behavior
  + stop I02 if validator configuration can retrieve external resources
  + stop I02 if an adversarial cycle can cause unbounded traversal or allocation

